"""
MT-SUPINN — Physics-Regularized Multi-Task Network
for Bearing RUL Prediction with Deep-Ensemble Conformal UQ

Known limitations (documented, not fixed — see paper Section "Limitations"):
  * Channel semantics are dataset-dependent. The model expects
    [vib, cur_1, cur_2, temp]. CWRU/Pronostia only provide vibration
    channels and are zero-padded into the current/temperature slots.
    The "current" branch therefore processes accelerometer data for
    those datasets. Do NOT interpret per-branch results as modality
    attribution.
  *  * The RUL target is a power law y(τ) = 1 − τ^α with per-bearing α
    fitted from the late-life RMS slope. Because the target is EXACTLY
    Paris-shaped (dD/dτ = C · D^m with C = α, m = (α−1)/α analytically),
    (C, m) are set in closed form and no LSQ is performed. The prior
    is therefore not fit to the target — it is derived from it.
    Remaining limitation: m < 1 for any α-scaled target; per-bearing m
    lies in [0.231, 0.667].
  * RUL is predicted from single 1024-sample windows (0.04 s at 25.6 kHz).
    No temporal context across the run. Comparisons with trajectory-level
    models (e.g. BiLSTM over the whole degradation sequence) are not
    like-for-like.
  * MC-dropout passes run with training=True, which places BatchNorm
    in batch-statistics mode. Reported as a limitation.
  * Sample size (3 train / 1 val / 2 test bearings) is small; leave-one-
    bearing-out CV is the recommended evaluation but is not implemented
    here.
"""

